% references.bib -- verified bibliography for the Typical / System-One decision-model paper.
%
% PROVENANCE. Every entry below was machine-fetched, never hand-written:
%   1. work located via the OpenAlex works API (or ACL Anthology / arXiv API), then
%   2. the BibTeX itself retrieved by DOI content negotiation:
%        curl -sLH "Accept: application/x-bibtex" https://doi.org/<doi>
%      (CrossRef for publisher DOIs, DataCite for 10.48550/arXiv.* DOIs), or
%      https://aclanthology.org/<id>.bib for ACL Anthology entries.
%   3. the fetched title was string-matched against the intended title (Jaccard >= 0.6);
%      10 fuzzy-search mismatches were caught this way and re-fetched by exact identifier.
% dblp.org (and its uni-trier / dagstuhl mirrors) was unusable: all three are behind an
% Anubis proof-of-work bot wall that returns an HTML challenge to curl.
%
% CAVEATS for the paper writer:
%   * the misc/arXiv entries carry the preprint year; many appeared later at ICLR/NeurIPS/ACL.
%     Upgrade to the venue entry before submission where the venue matters.
%   * A few CrossRef titles contain HTML markup (e.g. <i>...</i> in jiang2021calibration)
%     and SHOUTING CAPS (brier1950verification, murphy1970rps) -- strip/normalise at use time.
%   * Keys follow {firstauthor}{year}{keyword}; 11 keys were aligned to the spellings already
%     cited in paper/sections/*.tex (e.g. humeau2020polyencoders, wong2026models, zhao2021calibrate).
%   * Anything listed under "[VERIFY]" at the end of this file was NOT verified and MUST NOT be
%     cited as a BibTeX key.

